        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "This list identifies systems that require updates to meet current patch levels. These systems pose a security vulnerability within the SS&C network.\n\nThe Windows Infrastructure team schedules patching sessions every Saturday to address these systems in batches of 10.\n\nThe panel labeled \"Week 1\" represents the current week's patching efforts. Weeks 2-4 are displayed to allow product teams to anticipate upcoming systems. This list is updated daily; thus, the lineup of systems may change. Please ensure to review it regularly.\n\nSystems will be brought up to the current standard and may require multiple reboots. Change controls will be created and reviewed weekly in the Change Advisory Board (CAB) meetings.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "10.3.0",
